#
# Conformance case: transaction/protocol-strict-2pl.
#
# A logic:ConcurrentComposition whose run declares a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol
# (logic:declaredProtocol on its contract) and records the protocol's own events
# (per-leg logic:transactionTimestamp and/or per-action logic:lockAcquired /
# logic:lockReleased). The native evaluator classifies whether the witnessed
# schedule respects that protocol's discipline over those recorded events — a
# polynomial WELL-FORMEDNESS check (Principle 12), never a schedule search — and
# records the verdict as logic:protocolEnforced (with a logic:protocolViolationReason
# when the schedule breaks the discipline).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/protocol-strict-2pl/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

# The compile-time reasoning contract selects the transaction-path Evolution facet.
ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution .
